{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_00424f70d2434f055f11b1ff994f949cd23e94e408a6eacf795de303c955838e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a collection of extensions for pi, a terminal-based coding agent, organized as multiple packages."},{"claim_ids":["clm_72d4fe9ac55859f985700450edea67f20fb981b8d59252cdbed628c4fa57cf6d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The author describes this as a working collection rather than a polished suite; some extensions are daily tools, others experiments that may change or be dropped."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8fce552c5447e492958c5ad8e83416edd0da3eb349766f7330e98164f59c800a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Packages include pi-minimal-footer (footer with context gauge and usage bars), pi-session-recall (search past sessions), pi-auto-permissions, pi-codex-subagents, pi-codex-compaction, and pi-herdr-worktree-jump, all marked as core usage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_90070dab5e239d0fb698614233e501bb426c5e47f5b9294eab9794ff51a3fd4d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each package's own README contains its setup and usage instructions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_995a6176bd1d492c0330a1913d7fa8f129b3891c1fd3ec65383a31a35d0a6dce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Additional packages include pi-quit-and-delete and pi-ssh-tools (moderate tier) plus pi-fork-plus and pi-herdr (experimental tier); the pi-model-agents row is truncated so its tier is not evidenced."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d01f8cdba7dea4578cd3547ae73a0335750c1044029db0bdad79a0b3439bca2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Packages are installed via the command 'pi install npm:@ogulcancelik/<package-name>'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fe470b40854dd4c0d5a53cd6d64e378a6ccfc13a0748a4e0a90f187a16fb167c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The table ordering suggests a rough ranking by how actively the author uses each extension, from core to experimental."}],"claim_ids":["clm_00424f70d2434f055f11b1ff994f949cd23e94e408a6eacf795de303c955838e","clm_72d4fe9ac55859f985700450edea67f20fb